          "ruleId": "CWE-798",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Default admin credentials (admin@example.com / Admin1234!) baked into production deploy scripts and public docs\n\nThe production deployment scripts hardcode a default administrator account (`admin@example.com` / `Admin1234!`) and set its bcrypt password hash directly in the database. The credential is publicly documented in the repository's deployment README and fork guide. Combined with the security group default that allows HTTP/HTTPS from `0.0.0.0/0` and a self-signed TLS certificate, any deployment produced by these scripts is trivially loggable by anyone who reads the public documentation, until an operator manually changes the password."
