            "text": "Cognito first-login email binding enables account takeover via unverified email claim\n\nOn first Cognito login, the backend binds a verified id_token to an existing local profile by matching the token's email claim against `profiles.username` and reassigns all of that profile's rows (memberships, chats, API keys, workflows) to the Cognito sub. If the user pool permits accounts whose email claim is not verified or is attacker-controlled, an attacker can take over any existing profile — including the admin — without knowing its password."
