          "message": {
            "text": "Shell command injection via unvalidated skill name in AgentCore container provisioning\n\nIn AgentCore runtime mode, skill names are interpolated unsanitized into shell commands executed inside the AgentCore runtime container. `runCommand(sessionId, \\`mkdir -p /workspace/.claude/skills/${skill.name}\\`)` builds a bash command from a skill name that is fully attacker-controlled (derived from an uploaded zip's directory name or the marketplace install reference), and the command wrapper only escapes single quotes and backslashes — so `;`, `$()`, and backticks pass through to `/bin/bash -c`, giving arbitrary command execution in the runtime container."
