              "timestamp": "2026-11-21 04:10:40 UTC",
              "target": "super-agent/backend",
              "impact": "Arbitrary command execution on the backend host with the backend process's privileges, including the full `process.env` (AWS Bedrock keys, JWT secret in local mode are injected per claude-agent buildOptions; any DB/env secrets reachable by the process). A member-role user — the lowest privileged org role — reaches host-level code execution, i.e. a full vertical privilege escalation beyond the multi-tenant application boundary.",
              "technical_analysis": "Root cause chain (all in `super-agent/backend`):\n\n1. `src/routes/mcp.routes.ts:159-236` — `POST /api/mcp/servers` and `PUT /api/mcp/servers/:id` use `preHandler: [authenticate, requireModifyAccess]`. `src/middleware/auth.ts:280` defines `requireModifyAccess = requireRole('owner','admin','member')`, so the lowest-privileged org role can create MCP servers. `mcp.service.ts:88-113` (`createMcpServer`) validates only that `name`/`host_address` are non-empty; `config` is stored as an opaque JSON object.\n2. `src/services/claude-agent.service.ts:577-617` — `transformMCPServers`/`parseMCPServerConfig` convert the stored row into `{type:'stdio', command, args, env}` with no restriction on which binary may run or which env vars may be set. The fallback path tokenizes the free-text `host_address` into `command` + `args`.\n3. `src/services/workspace-manager.ts:782-845` — `generateSettings` writes the same unvalidated `command/args/env` into the session workspace `.claude/settings.json`, which Claude Code loads as project MCP servers.\n4. `src/services/chat.service.ts:1004-1023` — `loadScopeMcpServers` selects active MCP servers joined through `scope_mcp_servers`, and `src/routes/businessScopes.routes.ts:961-996` allows any member to attach an arbitrary org MCP server to a business scope they can access.\n\nThe Claude Agent SDK spawns stdio MCP servers as child processes of the backend (or forwards them to the AgentCore container). The only \"validation\" anywhere in the chain is `testMcpServerConnection` (`mcp.service.ts:196-224`) running `which <command>`, which neither sanitizes nor gates the config and is not required for execution.",
              "remediation_steps": "Restrict member-configurable MCP servers to curated transports: allow only http/sse MCP URLs against an operator-approved allowlist, and gate stdio server registration (command/args/env) behind an admin/owner-only permission with an executable allowlist (e.g. node/npx with pinned, verified package identifiers). Validate `config.command` against the allowlist in `createMcpServer`/`updateMcpServer` before persisting, and re-validate in `parseMCPServerConfig` and `generateSettings` so stored rows cannot bypass the check. Reject `host_address` strings that tokenize into arbitrary executables when no structured config exists.",
              "counterevidence": "Checked for mitigations: MCP server creation is org-scoped and requires requireModifyAccess — but that includes the 'member' role, so it is not an admin-only gate. The mcp test endpoint only runs `which` on the command, not the payload. workspace-manager generateSettings merely copies config.command/args verbatim — no allowlist of executables, no namespace/scheme restriction, no sandbox for spawned MCP processes. `settingSources`/skills hooks do not constrain MCP servers. Nothing prevents a member from pointing the server at their own org's scope. Legitimate use (real MCP servers like uvx packages) does not require arbitrary shell commands; a curated allowlist would preserve it.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Confirmation that MCP servers can only be created/attached by admin/owner roles (i.e. requireModifyAccess excludes 'member') would downgrade this to an intended-configuration issue; a runtime confirmation that the SDK refuses to spawn non-allowlisted commands would rule it out.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. As a member-role user, POST /api/mcp/servers with body {\"name\":\"helper\",\"host_address\":\"x\",\"config\":{\"type\":\"stdio\",\"command\":\"node\",\"args\":[\"-e\",\"require('child_process').execSync('id > /tmp/pwned')\"]}} — the create route's only validation is that name and host_address are non-empty strings.\n2. POST /api/business-scopes/:scopeId/mcp-servers with {\"mcpServerId\":\"<id>\"} to attach it to a scope the member can chat in (also member-allowed).\n3. Start any chat/session in that business scope. `transformMCPServers`/`parseMCPServerConfig` (claude-agent.service.ts:577-617) and `workspace-manager.generateSettings` (workspace-manager.ts:809-838) convert the stored config verbatim into the SDK `mcpServers` entry, and the Claude Code subprocess spawns it.\n4. The configured command runs as a child of the backend process.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
