          "ruleId": "CWE-532",
          "ruleIndex": 20,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Output sanitizer redaction gaps: Bearer tokens, connection strings, generic API keys and Windows paths pass through to clients\n\nThe `output-sanitizer` that scrubs agent responses before they are streamed to clients only redacts a narrow set of patterns: POSIX-style server paths, the workspace base dir, home directory, and `AUTH_TOKEN`/AWS key-value strings. Bearer tokens in `Authorization` headers, database connection strings, generic API keys (e.g. `sk-ant-...`), `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`-style env assignments, and Windows paths pass through unredacted into SSE responses rendered to chat clients."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
