            "text": "Upload validation / unauthenticated access / content-type confusion — No issue identified: Avatar upload/serve (avatarService.ts, avatarRoutes.ts)\n\nUpload validates mimetype allowlist, re-encodes everything through sharp to 128x128 WebP (destroys any embedded payload), server-generated S3 key. GET /avatars/* has no authenticate preHandler (minor unauthenticated read of avatar objects, keys timestamp+random — low, noted) but content-type is forced to image/png|webp and the bucket is avatar-only; no stored-XSS or traversal (S3 keys, not FS paths). GET /avatars/presign/:key is authenticated; it can presign any key in the avatars bucket but that bucket holds only generated/re-encoded images."
